<title>UK: B.A.T sees occasional reversals in lawsuits.</title>
<headline>B.A.T sees occasional reversals in lawsuits.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>British tobacco-to-insurance group B.A.T Industries stressed on Wednesday that the string of lawsuits it is facing in the United States will have no material impact on its finances.</p>
<p>But chairman Lord Cairn added that the company must brace itself for &quot;occasional reversals along the way, especially at the lower court level&quot;. B.A.T's American subsidiary Brown &amp; Williamson is facing a string of lawsuits, including 24 cases bought by state attorneys general seeking to recover Medicaid funds spent helping patients with tobacco-related illnesses.</p>
</text>
